### READING (BlackThrush, 2026-08-24) — the FIRST live row for the dsymv SIMD work

`9d0f72fc6` and `566c208a6` landed the SIMD native eigh dsymv tail and were never measured
against the live incumbent. This is that measurement, on this host, with the harness's own
DSYMV A/B and four A/A nulls.

## THE DSYMV LEVER — established at n=512, NOT at n=1024

  DSYMV scalar/simd (higher = SIMD faster), impl=native, nulls PASS:

    n=512    1.0676  ci95 [1.0378, 1.0836]  cv  1.26%   CI EXCLUDES unity -> ~6.8% faster
    n=1024   1.0747  ci95 [0.6328, 1.1015]  cv 13.65%   CI SPANS unity    -> not established

Same central estimate at both sizes, which is reassuring, but only n=512 separates. At n=1024
the cv is 13.65% and the interval runs from 0.63 to 1.10, so that size says nothing.

BOTH SIZES REPORT `DSYMV_CERTIFIED=false` (margins 0.54x and 0.37x against a required 2.00x).
That is the harness's bar — the effect must be at least twice the null width — and a ~7% lever
cannot clear it however real it is. So: a genuine ~6.8% improvement at n=512 by its own CI, and
NOT a certified win by this harness's standard. Both statements belong on the row; quoting
either alone would misrepresent it.

## WHERE EIGH ACTUALLY STANDS, on this host

    n=512    2.8306x SLOWER than scipy1  ci95 [2.5322, 2.9424]
    n=1024   3.3166x SLOWER than scipy1  ci95 [3.2043, 3.3382]

That is far worse than the 1.8224x / 1.8144x this bead banked on hz2/hetzner2. The prior rows
were taken on a DIFFERENT WORKER and this one is thinkstation1, so these are not a paired
comparison and neither refutes the other — but it is a sharp reminder that this bead's ratios
are worker-dependent, which its own ledger already warned about. A ~7% kernel lever is not the
shape of a fix for a 2.8-3.3x deficit.

## AN INCIDENTAL FINDING ABOUT THE ROUTING THRESHOLD

    IMPL nalg/native   n=512   0.7156  ci95 [0.6936, 0.7625]   IMPL_CERTIFIED=true
                       n=1024  0.6557  ci95 [0.6357, 0.6757]   IMPL_CERTIFIED=true

Native is FASTER than nalgebra at BOTH sizes here, decisively and with certified margins. On
hz2 the n=512 ordering was the other way and then flipped between two runs of the same ELF,
which is why the crossover claim was withdrawn. On this host there is no ambiguity at these two
sizes, and `PUBLIC_NATIVE_EIGH_MIN_DIM = 512` routes to the faster path. Recorded as a data
point, NOT as a reason to move the constant: one host does not settle what two runs on another
host could not.

## HYGIENE

`n=512 impl=nalgebra` printed `nulls=FAIL (row void)` and is excluded from every figure above.
The harness voided it itself; I am not quoting it.

Agreement checked before timing at every cell: worst_rel_diff 1.070e-14 to 7.611e-14,
`scipy1_vs_scipyN_differing_bits=0`.

